<strong>PHP 8.5.12, 8.4.27, 8.3.36 and 8.2.35 fix two critical vulnerabilities that can allow unauthenticated remote code execution. All PHP users are strongly encouraged to update immediately.</strong>
</p><p><strong>Who is at risk:</strong> all PHP installations serving web requests, including PHP-FPM, Apache with mod_php, php-cgi, FrankenPHP and LiteSpeed. We consider the risk highest for mod_php, with a demonstrated exploit where an unauthenticated request can trigger the attack before any application code runs.</p><p class=\'fullArticleLink\'><a href=\'https://www.php.net/archive/2026.php#2026-10-21-5\' class>&hellip; read full article</a></p></div>',
